WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.285
Settle in bed or another safe resting place.

2
00:00:05.985 --> 00:00:18.400
This practice can support the transition toward sleep, but it cannot promise sleep or replace care for persistent sleep difficulty.

3
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.020
You do not need to finish the recording.

4
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:31.420
If you are awake at the end, nothing has gone wrong.

5
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:45.365
Adjust temperature, light, clothing, blankets, and position as much as you reasonably can.

6
00:00:47.065 --> 00:00:49.985
Let practical comfort come before meditation.

7
00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:05.297
Notice the places where the body meets the bed or support.

8
00:01:06.997 --> 00:01:18.912
Feel the broad contact of head, back, pelvis, legs, heels, arms, or whichever areas are resting.

9
00:01:32.888 --> 00:01:37.138
Let the surface carry its share of the weight.

10
00:01:38.838 --> 00:01:40.838
You do not need to become heavy.

11
00:01:42.538 --> 00:01:45.218
Notice where weight is already being received.

12
00:01:59.194 --> 00:02:01.554
Feel one ordinary breath.

13
00:02:03.254 --> 00:02:07.774
There is no special sleep breath to achieve.

14
00:02:09.474 --> 00:02:16.374
Let the inhale arrive in its own size and the exhale leave in its own time.

15
00:02:32.346 --> 00:02:34.106
Bring attention to the forehead.

16
00:02:35.806 --> 00:02:42.351
Notice warmth, coolness, pressure, movement, or little sensation.

17
00:02:44.051 --> 00:02:49.391
Let the muscles around the eyes do only the work they still need to do.

18
00:03:03.366 --> 00:03:05.566
Feel the jaw and mouth.

19
00:03:07.266 --> 00:03:13.126
If the teeth are touching with effort, allow a little space.

20
00:03:14.826 --> 00:03:20.552
Let the tongue find an easy place without arranging it precisely.

21
00:03:34.527 --> 00:03:36.687
Move awareness to the neck and shoulders.

22
00:03:38.387 --> 00:03:40.027
Imagine no change.

23
00:03:41.727 --> 00:03:48.457
Simply feel how these areas are positioned and where support reaches them.

24
00:04:04.429 --> 00:04:07.549
Notice both arms from shoulders to fingertips.

25
00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:13.329
Feel their length, temperature, and weight.

26
00:04:15.029 --> 00:04:18.874
One side may be clearer than the other.

27
00:04:34.847 --> 00:04:37.447
Let attention rest in the hands.

28
00:04:39.147 --> 00:04:46.512
Fingers may curl, spread, touch fabric, or remain difficult to feel.

29
00:04:48.212 --> 00:04:50.492
Nothing needs correcting.

30
00:05:06.464 --> 00:05:10.219
Bring awareness to the chest and upper back.

31
00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:18.859
Breathing moves through this region while the bed continues to hold the body.

32
00:05:20.559 --> 00:05:22.839
Let movement and support be known together.

33
00:05:40.808 --> 00:05:42.448
Notice the belly.

34
00:05:44.148 --> 00:05:50.518
It may rise, widen, settle, tighten, or remain subtle.

35
00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:54.378
Do not push it toward softness.

36
00:05:56.078 --> 00:05:59.518
Follow two ordinary breaths as they are.

37
00:06:19.483 --> 00:06:21.883
Feel the lower back and pelvis.

38
00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:31.198
This central weight may be broad, uneven, comfortable, restless, or numb.

39
00:06:32.898 --> 00:06:37.843
If an adjustment is needed, make it slowly and begin again.

40
00:06:53.815 --> 00:06:57.095
Move down through both thighs.

41
00:06:58.795 --> 00:07:02.995
Notice where they touch the bed and where there is space.

42
00:07:04.695 --> 00:07:10.335
Let the legs be supported without asking them to feel relaxed.

43
00:07:26.307 --> 00:07:31.712
Include the knees, lower legs, ankles, and feet.

44
00:07:33.412 --> 00:07:37.972
Sense the whole path from pelvis to toes.

45
00:07:39.672 --> 00:07:44.987
Temperature and pressure may change from one area to the next.

46
00:08:04.952 --> 00:08:08.828
Now feel the body as one resting shape.

47
00:08:10.528 --> 00:08:15.872
Some areas may be vivid and others almost absent.

48
00:08:17.572 --> 00:08:19.652
Let the map be incomplete.

49
00:08:39.618 --> 00:08:44.743
Sounds may continue inside or outside the room.

50
00:08:46.443 --> 00:08:55.143
Rather than waiting for perfect silence, let each sound appear and pass within a larger quiet.

51
00:09:13.112 --> 00:09:17.646
If thoughts about tomorrow arrive, notice planning.

52
00:09:19.346 --> 00:09:24.356
If thoughts about today arrive, notice remembering.

53
00:09:26.056 --> 00:09:30.406
You do not need to finish either activity now.

54
00:09:46.379 --> 00:09:52.919
Use a brief phrase if helpful: this can wait until waking.

55
00:09:54.619 --> 00:09:59.309
Repeat it once, then return to weight against the bed.

56
00:10:17.277 --> 00:10:22.367
Notice the darkness or dim light through the eyelids.

57
00:10:24.067 --> 00:10:33.797
Shapes, colors, movement, or plain darkness can drift without your attention following them.

58
00:10:51.766 --> 00:10:54.406
Let the breath become less interesting.

59
00:10:56.106 --> 00:11:00.581
You do not need to monitor every cycle.

60
00:11:02.281 --> 00:11:07.911
Feel only an occasional exhale, then return to the whole resting body.

61
00:11:29.873 --> 00:11:40.208
Perhaps sleepiness is present as heaviness, blurred thought, warmth, drifting images, or small gaps in attention.

62
00:11:41.908 --> 00:11:46.838
There is no need to check whether it is working.

63
00:12:06.803 --> 00:12:09.043
Perhaps wakefulness remains clear.

64
00:12:10.743 --> 00:12:19.353
Let wakefulness be a condition you are resting with, not an opponent you must defeat.

65
00:12:39.318 --> 00:12:43.988
For several moments, release the practice itself.

66
00:12:45.688 --> 00:12:49.814
No body scan, no counting, no task.

67
00:12:51.514 --> 00:12:58.414
Let the bed hold the body while sounds and breath continue without supervision.

68
00:13:26.365 --> 00:13:37.830
If attention gathers again, feel one broad area of contact: the back, side, legs, or head.

69
00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:41.810
Let that single fact be enough.

70
00:14:03.772 --> 00:14:05.372
You may stop listening now.

71
00:14:07.072 --> 00:14:10.857
There is nothing further you need to achieve.

72
00:14:12.557 --> 00:14:17.082
Sleep may come, or rest may continue as rest.

73
00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:51.750
If you remain awake and choose to move, do so gently and follow whatever sleep-care plan is appropriate for you.

74
00:14:53.450 --> 00:15:00.000
For now, let this moment be quiet, unfinished, and free from a test.
